From dac87d1c7d6272b69b94ebe8cbe2a1f95cacb9aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 08:15:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Altera logo, enlarge TSMC/Intel, add emoji accents to
 capability labels

- Rasterized altera.svg to a PNG at 1472x400 (via a headless render
  with a transparent background, so quality/colors are preserved).
  The source SVG itself checked out fine and rendered correctly in my
  own testing, but since it was reported broken/missing on the live
  site and I couldn't reproduce the failure, converting to PNG removes
  SVG rendering as a variable entirely rather than leaving it
  unresolved.
- TSMC and Intel logos are now larger than the rest of the strip
  (trust-logo-lg: 58px vs 44px desktop, 44px vs 34px mobile) -- TSMC
  in particular has fine detail that reads better at a larger size.
- Added a star accent to "Process nodes" and a heart accent to
  "Application fields" in the V-Chip at a glance panel, per the
  Xiaomi reference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SjcntVjf5Nr2bdomgFdfPu
